"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ed9e2006c040328f974fb958e30652dfdbe5a425236e141782ce0b7ed461d44d","event_uuid":"4ba2454a-7822-4eb9-b2b9-cb9a0a5546b0","position":{"commit_sha":"18c795359fa5636794654a9456d9dd9b25511845","position":"1789017207316148001-4ba2454a-7822-4eb9-b2b9-cb9a0a5546b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a14daf201b5d8e641dba74da60150debf9104c8186ce0252e27e3e96430a9db0","event_uuid":"ab91e945-0a72-4601-b398-6134eb8f17ff","position":{"commit_sha":"4138fd2e97347e466bfe674dc9a2a32b71e0666a","position":"1789017992792254001-ab91e945-0a72-4601-b398-6134eb8f17ff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"641f5f5c05bfd84d891178e19a9c9012bc68fc2c6a62be12ea42d9faec35dd88","event_uuid":"70768e79-e499-435e-afa6-c92d18748b9c","position":{"commit_sha":"e36ae36ff57b48fd9c573f7cba3de3256ef5fd25","position":"1789018039988794001-70768e79-e499-435e-afa6-c92d18748b9c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting implementation after plan-review PASS. RCA target: prevent repeat of the noolbenger repair error where mirror recovery wrote directly into Gerrit branch refs; implementing runbook + guard with RED tests first.","timestamp":1789007759068453001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation committed as ac93a8a7e311e after RED tests pinned the unsafe-repair class: runbook must use refs/recovery/github/* quarantine, invoke validate-gerrit-repair-refspecs.sh, reject +refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*, and run post-repair fsck/replication/Mirror Guard checks. Validation passed: targeted tests (tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py, 8 passed), shellcheck for the guard, and full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2.","timestamp":1789013918777313001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2956 merged at 2026-09-10 05:00:53Z as 8b256444eebc154d28724cedd3a3537cccf08b1e after LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, unresolved=0. GitHub mirror caught up to the same SHA. CI_RESULT: {\"run_id\":\"34436715190\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":1983,\"fixes_applied\":[],\"retry_count\":0}.","timestamp":1789017119868781001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788957301670991001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0570efd9-bd0c-49e5-99a9-b3d376ee4b08","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8c0b-7f16-1ea0-4afc"},{"link_uuid":"21c4d435-4830-4d6e-aaa8-56d6033ffe39","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3fd6-0b2e-5707-4019"}],"description":"## Context\nNoolbenger RCA found that a Gerrit object-store repair fetched the stale GitHub mirror directly into Gerrit branch refs (`+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*`), moving `refs/heads/main` backward while Gerrit NoteDb still marked later changes MERGED.\n\n## Plan\n1. Update `infra/runbooks/gerrit-object-store-repair.md` so repair fetches import objects only into a concrete quarantine namespace, `refs/recovery/github/*`, never directly into `refs/heads/*` or other live refs.\n2. Put the guard in the operator path: add `infra/scripts/validate-gerrit-repair-refspecs.sh` and have the runbook require operators to run it immediately before any manual mirror-recovery `git fetch`. The guard hard-rejects refspecs whose destination is `refs/heads/*`; warning-only behavior is not acceptable for protected branch refs.\n3. Extend `tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py`, the existing content contract for this runbook, with assertions for the quarantine namespace, forbidden direct-branch refspec, required pre/post checklist items, and guard behavior.\n4. Include pre/post checks in the runbook: EBS snapshot before mutation, record expected old/new main SHAs, fetch quarantine refs, verify named objects plus `refs/heads`, `refs/tags`, `refs/changes`, and `refs/meta`, run `git fsck --full --connectivity-only --no-dangling --strict`, trigger replication, run Mirror Guard merged-reachability, and only then retire the quarantine namespace.\n5. Verify locally with the RED test first, then targeted tests and `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2`; land through Gerrit and close after both gates pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The runbook names `refs/recovery/github/*` as the quarantine namespace for mirror-recovery imports.\n- [x] The runbook contains no repair refspec that writes mirror refs directly to `refs/heads/*`.\n- [x] The runbook requires `infra/scripts/validate-gerrit-repair-refspecs.sh` before any manual mirror-recovery `git fetch`.\n- [x] The guard hard-rejects the known-bad refspec `+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*`.\n- [x] The guard hard-rejects any refspec whose destination is `refs/heads/*`.\n- [x] The guard permits a quarantine refspec such as `refs/heads/main:refs/recovery/github/main`.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py` asserts the runbook quarantine namespace and checklist contract.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py` asserts guard reject/allow behavior.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes an EBS snapshot before mutation.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes recording expected old/new main SHAs before and after repair.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes verifying `refs/changes` and `refs/meta` reachability.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes `git fsck --full --connectivity-only --no-dangling --strict`.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes triggering Gerrit-to-GitHub replication after repair.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes running Mirror Guard merged-reachability after repair.\n- [x] The runbook checklist includes retiring `refs/recovery/github/*` only after verification succeeds, or deleting it on abort.\n- [x] The runbook links the repair checklist to the Mirror Guard merged-reachability invariant added during noolbenger.\n- [x] `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before Gerrit review.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/runbooks/gerrit-object-store-repair.md","reason":"Document quarantine-only mirror recovery refspec, backup/checklist, fsck and merged-reachability verification."},{"path":"infra/scripts/validate-gerrit-repair-refspecs.sh","reason":"Lightweight guard that rejects repair fetch refspecs writing to protected branch refs."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py","reason":"Regression tests for repair runbook and refspec guard."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3fd6-0b2e-5707-4019"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ab91e945-0a72-4601-b398-6134eb8f17ff","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["gerrit","runbook","integrity"],"ticket_id":"c8dc-9fb2-ddfa-45d0","ticket_type":"task","title":"Document safe Gerrit object-store repair","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f199e1ce-073b-4290-b074-f4b454cf18ce","872af1d2-8a91-489b-8746-e8b4376fae07","4e1acf07-47f4-40f1-8fe0-887895445ca5","42482cb9-8e0a-4d6f-9368-5a21acbc1748","2d48e5c6-7f18-40a2-8e7f-712d671ab2e0","52d252c8-b978-47ee-b615-7c25980064a3","c48e7a17-a5e1-4199-9d7a-96e13998e329","21c4d435-4830-4d6e-aaa8-56d6033ffe39","0606ca5b-469e-40a5-8e88-a97b5668bb70","4ba2454a-7822-4eb9-b2b9-cb9a0a5546b0","ab91e945-0a72-4601-b398-6134eb8f17ff","70768e79-e499-435e-afa6-c92d18748b9c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789021386414170664,"uuid":"94739538-ca81-4fce-a3e6-7388d1de1b6c"}